# /etc/sudoers.d/devlab-runs — Mercury autonomous-run install grant.
# Install with:  sudo install -o root -g root -m 0440 deploy/devlab-runs.sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/devlab-runs
# Validate with: sudo visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/devlab-runs
#
# devlabd (user `devlab`) may invoke ONLY the install wrapper as root. The wrapper is generic and
# install-only (validated artifact paths, inline root-owned templates) — it never executes
# repo-provided code as root, and there is no arbitrary sudo here.
#
# The grant presupposes the wrapper's namespace configuration: /etc/devlab/gh-owner must name the
# organisation whose repositories may be installed (the same value as the daemon's DEVLAB_GH_OWNER).
# Without it devlab-install refuses every foreign repository (exit 5) — the grant is then harmless
# but useless. It is deliberately a ROOT-OWNED FILE and not an environment variable: the caller of
# this grant must not be able to widen the namespace it is measured against.
#
# The runner user `devlab-runs` gets NO sudo at all — deliberately. An unattended agent running with
# `--permission-mode bypassPermissions` treats ANY sudo grant as arbitrary root: it can write a file
# and reach for an allowed command creatively (a systemd unit runs ExecStart as root; `apt-get install`
# runs maintainer scripts as root; option-injection through wildcards). A scoped allowlist therefore
# does NOT bound the blast radius the way it appears to — it is effectively full root for the agent.
# So the runner has none. The constitution's "passwordless sudo vorausgesetzt" governs INTERACTIVE
# implementation (a human is present); it does not extend to the unattended nightly runner. The one
# privileged step the runner legitimately needs — install — goes through the root `devlab-install`
# wrapper below (invoked by the `devlab` service, never by the agent's shell), which only ever
# installs validated artifacts from root-owned templates. If the runner ever needs a further privileged action (e.g. restart one
# named service to verify a change), add a NARROW dedicated wrapper for exactly that — never a raw
# `systemctl *` / `apt-get *` / `journalctl *` grant.
devlab ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/devlab-install
